  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "Let \\(f\\) be a function for which \\(f\\!\\left(\\dfrac{x}{3}\\right) = x^2 + x + 1.\\) Find the sum of all values of \\(z\\) for which \\(f(3z) = 7.\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-\\dfrac{1}{3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-\\dfrac{1}{9}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{9}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{3}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "-1/9"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12-2000-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Setting \\(\\dfrac{x}{3} = 3z\\) gives \\(x = 9z,\\) so \\[ \\begin{aligned} f(3z) &= (9z)^2 + 9z + 1 \\\\ &= 81z^2 + 9z + 1 \\\\ &= 7. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThis rearranges to \\(81z^2 + 9z - 6 = 0.\\)\n\nBy the sum-of-roots formula, the sum of the values of \\(z\\) is \\(-\\dfrac{9}{81} = -\\dfrac{1}{9}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "To evaluate \\(f(3z),\\) set \\(\\dfrac{x}{3} = 3z,\\) so \\(x = 9z\\)",
        "This gives a quadratic in \\(z\\); use the sum-of-roots formula \\(-\\dfrac{b}{a}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
